wer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383531} {:answer/id #uuid "7b00f634-9599-5965-8f40-9e6474ab0791" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383532} {:answer/id #uuid "f38e3aba-b47f-541c-aa66-da66bf8d1540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383533} {:answer/id #uuid "cfcbe347-2504-5975-baa3-b1307425330b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "817eea6b-4bcd-50a0-bd01-e9c9361a4607" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383531} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae626fe0-3107-5566-bc20-cde6cc1edd64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383529}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fff1ef63-7fa2-5e33-aa47-b4df6f56d662" :question/math-academy-id "q-161788" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{2}+v \\\\ 2u-{v}^{3}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}2u & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3{v}^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =2u\\cdot (-3{v}^{2})-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-6u{v}^{2}-2 \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,2)} & =(-6u{v}^{2}-2)\\,{|}_{u=1\\,v=2} \\\\  & =-6(1)(2)^{2}-2 \\\\  & =-26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-26|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =26\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129527 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dc7b2d-483b-5c21-bc52-af09b2738d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279050} {:answer/id #uuid "c1a09ab6-33e6-5ece-a662-897c11c5ccd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280292} {:answer/id #uuid "d69096ab-d2da-522b-a9e8-43b1733cab55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280486} {:answer/id #uuid "da3fef5b-3c5a-5bb3-87f5-3ea6a20ec484" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280518} {:answer/id #uuid "fed38294-cb1c-52e8-92ca-723bf52e3cde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280820}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34dc7b2d-483b-5c21-bc52-af09b2738d49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279050} :answer-field/id #uuid "41f8b0d5-fe40-59fc-a296-062330e0b4a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280944}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c116e20c-7c3c-5121-8057-e62b04b89e02" :question/math-academy-id "q-161832" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,5)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}(uv) \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{u} & \\frac{1}{v} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot 2uv-\\frac{1}{v}\\cdot {v}^{2} \\\\  & =2v-v \\\\  & =v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,5)} & =v\\,{|}_{u=1\\,v=5} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|5|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =5\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c1db1d-2cc0-5ac8-8f04-c8180becd16a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383542} {:answer/id #uuid "821cd8c6-8ff9-5da6-80d4-645283944e57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383543} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9f678f-6723-5d0a-aaf8-823aac52bf9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383544} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd393ca-0f85-5050-8edc-c100a9d38ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383545} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab28153-3505-5ac2-969c-4808d24a5d4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dd393ca-0f85-5050-8edc-c100a9d38ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383545} :answer-field/id #uuid "91eca270-f22e-5746-93f6-648d523d80f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383541}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7c1651a7-19c3-5fc6-882f-8612e069dc1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161831" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v{e}^{u} \\\\ u{e}^{v}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}v{e}^{u} & {e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{v} & u{e}^{v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v{e}^{u}\\cdot u{e}^{v}-{e}^{v}\\cdot {e}^{u} \\\\  & =uv{e}^{u+v}-{e}^{u+v} \\\\  & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-1,1)} & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v}\\,{|}_{u=-1\\,v=1} \\\\  & =(-1\\cdot 1-1){e}^{-1+1} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-2|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =2\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a27b376-f76e-5224-bd14-dcd0f58ef17d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279419} {:answer/id #uuid "6df88852-e281-540b-9be8-5da79ff04db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279592} {:answer/id #uuid "e29c7966-53cc-5a98-a45d-f216ac316386" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280594} {:answer/id #uuid "e5bf82bf-7ae4-51b0-8078-b62137d694c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280619} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ae113f-b190-5e88-a500-9aa18217b4af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280706}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6df88852-e281-540b-9be8-5da79ff04db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279592} :answer-field/id #uuid "150f9199-b68c-5aef-8efe-e079ecbd49f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280869}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9ee4cd0d-00ad-5fb0-be36-91eca3f6f7a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-161873" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{u}-v \\\\ {u}^{2}v\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}} & -1 \\\\ 2uv & {u}^{2}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\left(-\\frac{1}{{u}^{2}}\\right)\\cdot ({u}^{2})-2uv\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-1+2uv \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,2)} & =(-1+2uv)\\,{|}_{u=2\\,v=2} \\\\  & =-1+2(2)(2) \\\\  & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|7|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =7\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d9515a0-7aca-5bd0-93c2-b5138c7c3052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279294} {:answer/id #uuid "62fb6c42-d7b5-5116-b4d8-c608240b0020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279491} {:answer/id #uuid "65e00832-3370-516f-bf0e-931f9e463a62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279521} {:answer/id #uuid "c042a147-a78a-546c-adff-8d9859d6b5eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280284} {:answer/id #uuid "df364235-b831-5c0a-a5fa-907e835f3022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62fb6c42-d7b5-5116-b4d8-c608240b0020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279491} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c8c07a6-1fb4-5da8-abe5-ac2081b48db6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280937}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9201622d-d447-58b4-8006-2fbea11393d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161874" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(4,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{u}+{v}^{2} \\\\ uv\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & 2v \\\\ v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot u-v\\cdot 2v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{u}-2{v}^{2} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(4,2)} & ={\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{u}-2{v}^{2}\\,|}_{u=4\\,v=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{4}-2(2)^{2} \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-7|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =7\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281368 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018385f7-7519-5922-8545-718d1e4443e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278597} {:answer/id #uuid "09f72da4-93f7-5f6e-8f5c-7adf97a2d87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278688} {:answer/id #uuid "42229dfb-92db-527f-98d4-81e464debdce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279182} {:answer/id #uuid "5806f5cb-b442-516d-a7af-f295ed7a67a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279401} {:answer/id #uuid "b63f49ff-6805-5e3d-9a84-bb5bf0cb46d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09f72da4-93f7-5f6e-8f5c-7adf97a2d87b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278688} :answer-field/id #uuid "30341de0-d7c9-531a-935d-0764a34a14a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280923}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8a571cf4-d621-5149-95d3-896e62b990d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161875" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(0,3)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}u-{v}^{2} \\\\ u+v\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & -2v \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-2v) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(0,3)} & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u+2v)\\,{|}_{u=0\\,v=3} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+2(3) \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|6|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =6\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6868218d-e1cc-5d50-a993-c991f43b1d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279541} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc9479c-c9e8-5ef9-bf90-29e06a33263c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279705} {:answer/id #uuid "9162be54-7854-53e2-9565-c82bf2b82b2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279888} {:answer/id #uuid "d5ff9956-5830-5df1-9e06-3627aaf262d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280480} {:answer/id #uuid "d96ff063-ffb7-5f8f-95e7-79745e683d0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6868218d-e1cc-5d50-a993-c991f43b1d4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279541} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf437f98-16a0-57d1-a983-d2d8546f1bd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281197}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4a48d509-ce9f-57c3-ab71-29eb65410f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-161885" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,4)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ uv\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{2u}{v} & -\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}} \\\\ v & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2u}{v}\\cdot u-v\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{{u}^{2}}{{v}^{2}}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{u}^{2}}{v}+\\frac{{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,4)} & =\\left(\\frac{3{u}^{2}}{v}\\right)\\,{|}_{u=2\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3(2)^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|3|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =3\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cbff252-78de-56e0-9831-68d0d5847cf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278858} {:answer/id #uuid "254166ee-c366-5b0a-8254-ef1c99d8cefa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278923} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7b2391-4ac4-5aba-b7fd-d5c4a0c731ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279258} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb16338-8739-5100-afb4-a97df7a35f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279437} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec2c7bb-fc96-59d3-9cef-a3d5103aac04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bb16338-8739-5100-afb4-a97df7a35f4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279437} :answer-field/id #uuid "82c1b0c7-bd87-588b-918a-c6b0538039e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281069}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "787ef4d5-9dfe-5be7-87e1-4a46bed285bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-161887" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,4)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{uv} \\\\ u{v}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\ {v}^{2} & 2uv\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{v}}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot 2uv-{v}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{u}}{2\\sqrt{v}} \\\\  & =v\\sqrt{uv}-\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(1,4)} & ={(\\frac{1}{2}v\\sqrt{uv})\\,|}_{u=1\\,v=4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(4)\\sqrt{(1)(4)} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|4|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =4\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383568 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f94640a-439d-5450-b89c-214d6351fa55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383570} {:answer/id #uuid "22b7af57-2308-539f-b4dc-7bf734738b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383571} {:answer/id #uuid "305c7067-b121-52de-832b-2cd582abe378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383572} {:answer/id #uuid "0e57c966-7e8f-5c20-b14e-3fff17deba68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383573} {:answer/id #uuid "c14d8db9-1f54-501a-a0d4-dbdd47484709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383574}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "305c7067-b121-52de-832b-2cd582abe378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383572} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd0ed70-8ad1-5612-8701-9b382b52743e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383569}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f0941ca-edd5-5538-8a0c-b3d25f8e41f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-161877" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(2,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{ln}(u-v) \\\\ v-{u}^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{u-v} & -\\frac{1}{u-v} \\\\ -2u & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u-v}\\cdot 1-(-2u)\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{u-v}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2u}{u-v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(2,1)} & ={\\left(\\frac{1-2u}{u-v}\\right)\\,|}_{u=2\\,v=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2(2)}{2-1} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-3|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =3\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383575 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61164a03-d653-5509-8896-92a9f5d833f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383577} {:answer/id #uuid "5766d69f-6242-5cfa-96ee-c8cd587905ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383578} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec2c14a-52b6-5478-a60f-1f678392ec7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383579} {:answer/id #uuid "5317cbac-448e-539f-b6c8-0a7df3081b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383580} {:answer/id #uuid "18259f51-378f-592e-be8d-c8109a57fd90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5766d69f-6242-5cfa-96ee-c8cd587905ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383578} :answer-field/id #uuid "c852d323-c95a-5a6d-9333-8d677385a559" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383576}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3a2efb4f-04d0-536e-850b-89df0bdf4245" :question/math-academy-id "q-161878" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-3,3)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+{v}^{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}(u+v)\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2v \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\cdot 2v \\\\  & =(1-2v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v) \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-3,3)} & =(1-2v)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(u+v)\\,{|}_{u=-3\\,v=3} \\\\  & =(1-2(3))\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3+3) \\\\  & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-5|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =5\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186389216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efa02fb0-8bd7-58b2-846f-b834fa4d00a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389218} {:answer/id #uuid "f26a101a-d1b7-54cb-9da6-045b68d673b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389219} {:answer/id #uuid "102a5894-9256-52e2-86ff-598cf595625d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389220} {:answer/id #uuid "a7e6000c-9905-5a76-9098-325dd8f54c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389221} {:answer/id #uuid "eca4c4f3-4d0e-5221-a6c4-b18b4d27e0a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7e6000c-9905-5a76-9098-325dd8f54c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389221} :answer-field/id #uuid "c652ad8c-b6bc-516a-b0a9-9d72286277e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186389217}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dc1b537d-1bb4-5840-be74-781a73ccdf95" :question/math-academy-id "q-161876" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{u+v} \\\\ {u}^{3}+v\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{u+v} & {e}^{u+v} \\\\ 3{u}^{2} & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}\\cdot 1-3{u}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{u+v} \\\\  & ={e}^{u+v}(1-3{u}^{2}) \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-2,2)} & ={e}^{u+v}(1-3{u}^{2})\\,{|}_{u=-2\\,v=2} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2+2}(1-3(-2)^{2}) \\\\  & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-11|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =11\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502096 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0edfd29e-3a12-5f5c-aa4d-c9d232e9d8ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501491} {:answer/id #uuid "10477c22-e6c0-5396-865c-7efb2e452797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501495} {:answer/id #uuid "1354d1db-51ab-5f5c-944c-79110ffcc91b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501502} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba7e918-0922-576c-91b5-2e38e5a1b977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501571} {:answer/id #uuid "84d571a0-192f-5d6b-bfdc-6b4cf1be9b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84d571a0-192f-5d6b-bfdc-6b4cf1be9b9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501720} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a680a9f-c944-5dc6-b6be-a4a3dda024b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502031}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d5c488c-135d-5c5b-b6fb-380729a9e440" :question/math-academy-id "q-161886" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(3,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{3}-v \\\\ v-u\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}-1 \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(3,1)} & =(3{u}^{2}-1)\\,{|}_{u=3\\,v=1} \\\\  & =3(3)^{2}-1 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|26|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =26\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10c25e88-eda6-5994-8669-2fc4e8989223" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{80}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518907} {:answer/id #uuid "2938687d-5d55-5245-8c65-6f9840dccd9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "160\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518914} {:answer/id #uuid "3f0938ab-55ed-5367-8d20-ae9cdfd95ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518920} {:answer/id #uuid "a3238964-bd1d-5761-80d6-d8671006ef6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6400\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518951} {:answer/id #uuid "b76da343-223a-5697-a37a-50a8d039196b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f0938ab-55ed-5367-8d20-ae9cdfd95ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "80\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518920} :answer-field/id #uuid "f13aea66-5851-5988-acfe-308733165daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518972}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "14ceb78e-322f-54a1-9174-9de018a820b6" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,2)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 u v^{3}\\\\3 u^{2} + v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}2 v^{3}&6 u v^{2}\\\\6 u&2 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(2 v^{3})\\cdot (2 v)-(6 u v^{2})\\cdot (6 u)\\\\& =- 36 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{4}\\\\& =- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-1,2)} & =\\left(- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u - v\\right) \\left(3 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-1,v=2}\\\\& =- 4 (2)^{2} \\left(3 (-1) - (2)\\right) \\left(3 (-1) + (2)\\right)\\\\& =-80\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-80|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =80\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68183119-0e35-5d48-af62-a8b0b531100a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "192\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518936} {:answer/id #uuid "6abf04e2-7547-5fd6-adf1-679bbe9324da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{96}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518939} {:answer/id #uuid "a3594f26-df2d-522d-8678-6bd28bc24f8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9216\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518952} {:answer/id #uuid "b0631b4b-2af0-51ae-9938-eed818a10498" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518957} {:answer/id #uuid "d956c4c8-a269-5eba-9d74-d31be57b55d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d956c4c8-a269-5eba-9d74-d31be57b55d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "96\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518965} :answer-field/id #uuid "d765db19-5dd7-5fc5-8884-f5f88ec83632" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518964}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2f65179e-ed0f-5b0a-a190-a9cd8645ec56" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-3,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{2}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{2}&6 u v\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{2})\\cdot (4 v)-(6 u v)\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 12 u^{2} v + 12 v^{3}\\\\& =- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-3,-1)} & =\\left(- 12 v \\left(u - v\\right) \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-3,v=-1}\\\\& =- 12 (-1) \\left(- (-1) + (-3)\\right) \\left((-1) + (-3)\\right)\\\\& =96\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|96|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =96\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb