erefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|180|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =180\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15dbf132-3e31-59b6-b187-892685acc97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "88\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518909} {:answer/id #uuid "697e6aef-9964-5053-b382-5c88b21c2920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518937} {:answer/id #uuid "83524c04-5468-53fa-bd7d-bb4999cc9585" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1936\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518945} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d2a6d9-d644-5d45-8bdf-1c1fb6df4980" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518953} {:answer/id #uuid "f639046b-b2fc-5455-96d0-1286ffd8950a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{44}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "697e6aef-9964-5053-b382-5c88b21c2920" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "44\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518937} :answer-field/id #uuid "535e0d1f-0eed-5a50-9f3c-40a846b5562f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518929}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "adc92b5f-6402-53d1-8666-3baacdfe2c66" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-2,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}2 v^{3}&6 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&2 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(2 v^{3})\\cdot (2 v)-(6 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 12 u^{2} v^{2} + 4 v^{4}\\\\& =- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(-2,-1)} & =\\left(- 4 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=-2,v=-1}\\\\& =- 4 (-1)^{2} \\left(- (-1)^{2} + 3 (-2)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-44\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-44|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =44\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518958 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ec1407-5d3e-572e-b894-a96fde5d8e98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "75\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518912} {:answer/id #uuid "33d42482-34ef-59e1-9d7b-c0a1dcf6db23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "300\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518916} {:answer/id #uuid "39480101-3dbb-5f98-9d35-a02e91aadd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518917} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0670ce-c1db-5e79-a6f4-2e53c985344b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{150}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518919} {:answer/id #uuid "3ffa3aa9-000d-52d4-8910-4d539df8e087" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22500\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "39480101-3dbb-5f98-9d35-a02e91aadd76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518917} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae334581-cc02-5854-80ac-65ba5fd211c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518956}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b11a00bf-ad16-5270-bbbf-f403e6fe76c2" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(3,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}3 u v^{3}\\\\u^{2} + 2 v^{2}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}3 v^{3}&9 u v^{2}\\\\2 u&4 v\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(3 v^{3})\\cdot (4 v)-(9 u v^{2})\\cdot (2 u)\\\\& =- 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 12 v^{4}\\\\& =- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(3,1)} & =\\left(- 6 v^{2} \\left(3 u^{2} - 2 v^{2}\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=3,v=1}\\\\& =- 6 (1)^{2} \\left(- 2 (1)^{2} + 3 (3)^{2}\\right)\\\\& =-150\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-150|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =150\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a46dd2e-7844-511c-8225-1d0a51bb3eaf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "72\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518918} {:answer/id #uuid "421250cd-a2d2-59cf-a6de-47aaded334b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20736\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518922} {:answer/id #uuid "549b51aa-02b7-56c9-a3ea-cc9c797d0dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{144}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518931} {:answer/id #uuid "5c59fc35-b29f-5893-8340-a07c39c6bbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518933} {:answer/id #uuid "ec16d3f2-9da5-5e85-813f-086fbb3e74c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "288\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c59fc35-b29f-5893-8340-a07c39c6bbb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "144\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518933} :answer-field/id #uuid "e48954b8-5146-577a-919f-6d9a5e7fbd72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dcaa4bdd-7f4f-5106-9de8-2ca23f1745cd" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(1,-1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}\\longrightarrow\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\left(2 u + v\\right)^{2}\\\\\\left(u - v\\right)^{3}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))\\approx\\left|\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|\\cdot\\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial x}{\\partial v}\\\\\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial u}&\\frac{\\partial y}{\\partial v}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =\\begin{vmatrix}8 \\left(2 u + v\\right)&4 \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}&- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2}\\end{vmatrix}\\\\& =(8 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (- 3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})-(4 \\left(2 u + v\\right))\\cdot (3 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2})\\\\& =- 72 u^{3} + 108 u^{2} v - 36 v^{3}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\\\\\left.\\frac{\\partial(x,y)}{\\partial(u,v)}\\right|_{(1,-1)} & =\\left(- 36 \\left(u - v\\right)^{2} \\left(2 u + v\\right)\\right)\\big|_{u=1,v=-1}\\\\& =- 36 \\left(- (-1) + (1)\\right)^{2} \\left((-1) + 2 (1)\\right)\\\\& =-144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & \\approx|-144|\\cdot\\delta A\\\\ & =144\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Local Area Scale Factor of a Transformation"}]}
